			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2807544">
									

<p>On my first read-through I thought the anomaly was duplicating or modifying the tea types taped to the wall. I think the difficulty is that both the collected, dried tea leaves and the potable solution produced by steeping said leaves can both be referred to as &quot;tea&quot;. Perhaps bumping up the science jargon in this regard would be appropriate? YMMV</p>
<p>I wonder about the tea in the pot - does it stay hot until drunk? Does it remain hot when removed from the classroom, ie. is the hot tea itself anomalous?</p>
<p>And the entity that makes it all happen, would she mark/edit a paper left behind with a nice bag of tea? What would it take for her to give a &quot;F - SEE ME AFTER CLASS&quot; kind of response?</p>
<p>I think you can push the premise of this SCP, and look forward to seeing you do it.</p>

